The attached image illustrates the physical characteristics of Nano-11 nanoparticles. Panel A displays a Transmission Electron Microscopy (TEM) image, showing spherical particles with irregular, cauliflower-like surfaces, consistent with their dendrimer-like nature, with a 50 nm scale bar. Panel B presents the size distribution of Nano-11 as determined by dynamic light scattering, indicating a relatively uniform Z-average hydrodynamic diameter ranging from 75 to 80 nm. This characterization confirms the morphology and size of the α-D-glucan nanoparticles, which are engineered for their role as vaccine adjuvants.